# Per-session linked feature worktrees (`AGENTS.md` "Hard Cutover by Default"
# mandates `.claude/worktrees/<slug>/`). Per-session, per-machine ephemeral
# state — like `.check/` and `scratchpad/` in the charly repo, it lives in the
# project tree but stays OUT of git. Without this entry a checkout that follows
# the mandated worktree convention reads dirty, and the umbrella's
# `scripts/verify-pins.sh` fails with `FAIL: <repo>: dirty working tree`.
.claude/worktrees/

# `charly check run` writes its run evidence under .check/<bed>/<calver>/, and the R10 bed's
# `charly vm build` writes the built disk + seed ISO under image/<entity>/ — both are GENERATED
# evidence, and neither ever belongs in git (the disk alone is megabytes).
.check/
image/
